=== company.md ===
---
description: Company overview, systems and URLs, naming conventions
---
# CentrAlign (sandbox company)
We are a small company that processes vendor invoices and purchase orders.

## Systems
- Internal ERP (mock): http://127.0.0.1:5001
  - The browser session is already logged in. Never log in; if you land on /login the tools re-authenticate automatically.
  - Vendors: /vendors, Invoices: /invoices, New invoice: /invoices/new
  - Purchase orders: /pos, PO detail: /pos/<id>
- Source documents are local files under `sandbox/data/`:
  - `sandbox/data/invoices/`  vendor invoice PDFs, named `<vendor-slug>_<invoice-no>.pdf`
  - `sandbox/data/purchase_orders/`  PO PDFs, named `<vendor-slug>_<po-no>.pdf`
  - `sandbox/data/emails/`  vendor emails, named `<vendor-slug>_<invoice-no>.txt`; some invoices arrive only as emails
    (same fields as the PDF invoices: Invoice No, Invoice Date, Due Date, Amount Due)

## Conventions
- Amounts are entered as plain numbers with two decimals, no currency symbol or commas (e.g. 3480.00).
- Dates: the ERP requires YYYY-MM-DD even though the form label says MM/DD/YYYY.
- Always use the vendor's canonical name from the vendor list.
- "Latest" means the most recent date printed inside the document, not the file name or file time.

=== policies.md ===
---
description: Approval thresholds and what the AI may and may not do
approval_threshold: 5000
allowed_urls: http://127.0.0.1:5001
allowed_paths: sandbox/data
---
# Policies
- Invoices with an amount above the approval threshold (USD 5,000) need recorded human approval before they are submitted. The system blocks the submit until approval is recorded.
- If the vendor name is ambiguous (matches more than one vendor), ask the human which one. Never guess.
- If several invoices could be "the latest" (same date), ask the human.
- The AI may only open URLs on the allow-list and read files under the allowed paths.
- The AI must never submit the same invoice twice. If the ERP reports a duplicate, stop and report it.
- The AI must not change or delete existing ERP records.

=== procedures/invoice_entry.md ===
---
description: Step-by-step procedure for entering a vendor invoice into the ERP
---
# Procedure: enter a vendor invoice
1. Confirm the vendor with `lookup_vendor`. If it reports AMBIGUOUS, ask the human (needs_human) and do not continue.
2. Call `find_latest_document(kind="invoice", vendor=<canonical name>)`. It searches invoice PDFs and invoice emails and
   picks the latest by the date printed inside each file. If it reports AMBIGUOUS (several share the latest date), ask the human.
3. `read_file` the returned source_file and extract: invoice_number, amount (Amount Due, numeric only), due_date. Report them in the step result facts.
4. Open `/invoices/new`.
5. Fill vendor, invoice number, amount, due date using `fill_form`, then call `submit_record` with record_type="invoice".
